Seers' Ops

A hands-on lab that simulates a real-world infrastructure to put HolmesGPT, an open-source AI troubleshooting agent, to work as an on-call investigator.

Everything runs on a local kind Kubernetes cluster that sets up with a single command on Windows, macOS or Linux. A simulator app breaks things on purpose (broken deployments, network issues, crash loops and more), it's shipped through GitHub Actions and ArgoCD, and an open-source observability stack gives HolmesGPT the evidence it needs to find the root cause.

Built in three sprints by a small team practicing real engineering workflows: planning, reviews and decisions documented along the way.

Roadmap
Sprint 1 - Foundation: local kind cluster and cross-OS automated setup
Sprint 2 - Simulation: failure simulator app, CI/CD and GitOps
Sprint 3 - Investigation: observability stack and HolmesGPT
